423
00:39:07,756 --> 00:39:16,756
While we wait for our food... But we should also give you... since you're turning Indonesian, we need to give you an Indonesian introduction. -Oh, yeah! How to do that?

424
00:39:17,256 --> 00:39:24,756
So can you say your introduction just in your normal...? -Haachama-chama~! Worldwide-traveling idol, Akai Haato!

425
00:39:25,256 --> 00:39:28,756
So in Indonesian, that would be...

426
00:39:28,756 --> 00:39:48,756
Haachama-chama! Idola... yang... menjelajahi... dunia... Akai Haato!

427
00:39:49,256 --> 00:40:02,256
Menjelajahi dunia Akai Haato... What was the first word? -Idola... -Idola yang menjelajahi... -dunia... -dunia! Idola yang menjelajahi...

428
00:40:02,264 --> 00:40:03,564
Idola yang menjelajahi dunia!
The world-exploring idol...

429
00:40:03,564 --> 00:40:04,664
Akai Haato!

430
00:40:08,064 --> 00:40:10,764
料理の準備ができたみたい！
Oh, it looks like our food is on the way!

431
00:40:10,964 --> 00:40:12,264
お腹も空いてるし
I'm starting to get hungry.

432
00:40:12,264 --> 00:40:13,964
さっそく食べましょう〜！
Let's eat!

433
00:40:16,564 --> 00:40:20,164
Okay, our first dish has arrived. This is tempe!
Okay, our first dish has arrived. This is tempeh!

434
00:40:21,664 --> 00:40:22,864
Are you hungry?

435
00:40:22,864 --> 00:40:24,764
I'm hungry!

436
00:40:25,264 --> 00:40:29,264
こちらがテンペのソースだよ
And this is the sauce that they give...

437
00:40:29,264 --> 00:40:31,064
Dipして食べようね
...yeah, so we can dip and eat it.

438
00:40:31,264 --> 00:40:32,464
このソースは甘いの？
Is this sauce sweet?

439
00:40:32,464 --> 00:40:34,664
甘いのかな？辛いのかな？
Mmm, I wonder... Is it sweet or spicy?

440
00:40:35,264 --> 00:40:37,264
お箸とスプーンが手元にあるんだけど
We have chopsticks and spoons here...

441
00:40:37,264 --> 00:40:40,464
スタッフが手で食べてもいいって言うから手で食べるね
...but staff said we can eat with our hands, so I'll eat with my hands.

442
00:40:43,764 --> 00:40:45,964
まずはソースなしで食べているよ
So first, I'll try without the sauce.

443
00:40:46,264 --> 00:40:48,764
私も食べてみるね ソースにつけよう
I'll try dipping it in the sauce.

444
00:40:54,764 --> 00:40:58,064
ソースは甘さのある味だね
The sauce has a sweet flavor, right?

445
00:40:58,764 --> 00:41:00,464
これも試していい？
Can I try this one too?

446
00:41:00,464 --> 00:41:01,464
辛いソースだね！
It's a spicy sauce!

447
00:41:02,564 --> 00:41:08,064
別に用意してもらったソースなんだけど多分結構辛いよ
They prepared a separate sauce for us, but it's probably pretty spicy.

448
00:41:08,264 --> 00:41:10,264
さっそく食べてみよう
Let's try it right away!

449
00:41:13,064 --> 00:41:14,564
Gimana, Haachama?
How is it, Haachama?

450
00:41:17,264 --> 00:41:20,264
お箸で救出しよう
Let me rescue it with chopsticks.

451
00:41:23,764 --> 00:41:26,264
We can rescue it with chopsticks.

452
00:41:26,764 --> 00:41:28,264
It's spicy!

453
00:41:28,764 --> 00:41:29,764
I like it!

454
00:41:29,764 --> 00:41:32,264
普通のソースより辛っ
Spicier than the regular sauce!

455
00:41:35,264 --> 00:41:37,264
辛さが伝わったでしょ(笑)
You can tell how spicy it is, right? (Laughs)

456
00:41:38,064 --> 00:41:39,264
どっちのソースが好きだった？
Which sauce did you like better?

457
00:41:39,264 --> 00:41:40,764
辛い方！
The spicy one!

458
00:41:41,064 --> 00:41:43,264
はあちゃまは辛いのが好きだね〜
Haachama loves spicy food, huh~

459
00:41:44,764 --> 00:41:48,264
The next one we have Tahu Isi.
Next, we have Tahu Isi.

460
00:41:48,264 --> 00:41:49,264
Tahu Isi.

461
00:41:49,264 --> 00:41:52,264
豆腐を揚げてあるんだよ
They fried the tofu...

462
00:41:52,464 --> 00:41:54,764
すごくクリスピーだよ！
It's super crispy!

463
00:41:57,064 --> 00:41:59,064
Oh, it sounds good.

464
00:41:59,464 --> 00:42:03,264
この豆腐を開いてみるとね…
If you open up this tofu...

465
00:42:05,264 --> 00:42:07,764
の中に詰めてあるんだね
See, it's stuffed inside.

466
00:42:10,264 --> 00:42:15,064
もやしやにんじんなどの野菜が詰めてあるから
It's stuffed with vegetables like bean sprouts and carrots...

467
00:42:15,064 --> 00:42:17,264
ぜひ食べてみて〜
...so definitely try it!

468
00:42:17,764 --> 00:42:19,764
半分こする？
Want to split it in half?

469
00:42:21,764 --> 00:42:24,764
この辛いソースとすごく合うと思うよ
I think it goes really well with this spicy sauce.

470
00:42:29,764 --> 00:42:31,764
Spicy... Spicy...

471
00:42:32,764 --> 00:42:36,264
はあちゃまもインドネシアスタイルで手で食べてるね
Look, Haachama is also eating Indonesian style with her hands.

472
00:42:42,264 --> 00:42:45,264
もちもち
Oh, it's chewy, a little bit.

473
00:42:46,264 --> 00:42:49,764
このソース思ってたよりだいぶ辛いよ
This sauce is way spicier than I thought.

474
00:42:50,264 --> 00:42:53,264
The more you eat, the spicier it gets!

475
00:42:53,764 --> 00:42:54,764
Yeah, exactly!!!

476
00:42:55,264 --> 00:42:58,764
結構辛いな〜と思って食べているとどんどん辛さが広がってくる
You eat thinking it's pretty spicy, and the spiciness just keeps spreading.

477
00:42:59,264 --> 00:43:02,764
インドネシアに行けばどこでも見かけるんだけど
You can see this anywhere if you go to Indonesia...

478
00:43:06,764 --> 00:43:08,764
例えば屋台とか
...like at food stalls...

479
00:43:09,264 --> 00:43:15,764
屋台や道路端で気軽に買えるインドネシアで親しまれているストリートフードだよ
It's a popular street food in Indonesia that you can easily buy at stalls or on the roadside.

480
00:43:16,264 --> 00:43:18,264
屋台に行ってみたいな〜
I want to go to a street stall~

481
00:43:18,264 --> 00:43:19,764
Yeah~

482
00:43:20,764 --> 00:43:22,764
Okay, next!

483
00:43:22,764 --> 00:43:24,264
Next one!

484
00:43:26,764 --> 00:43:29,264
This is called Ayam Sisit.

485
00:43:29,264 --> 00:43:30,264
Ayam Sisit.

486
00:43:32,264 --> 00:43:39,264
茹でたり揚げたりした鶏肉を細かく裂いて香り豊かなスパイスで味付けした料理ね
It's a dish of shredded boiled or fried chicken seasoned with rich, aromatic spices.

487
00:43:39,764 --> 00:43:46,464
細かくほぐしてあるから味がよく染み込んでいて
It's shredded finely so the flavor soaks in really well.

488
00:43:46,764 --> 00:43:53,264
Bumbu Genepというペーストが使われているの
It uses a paste called Bumbu Genep.

489
00:43:53,764 --> 00:43:57,764
多分さっきのソースほど辛くはないはず
It's probably not as spicy as the previous sauce.

490
00:43:58,264 --> 00:44:00,064
きっと大丈夫
It should be fine.

491
00:44:00,264 --> 00:44:05,764
普段はライスと一緒に食べる料理なんだけどおそらくライスを一緒に出されていない理由は
Normally this dish is eaten with rice, but the reason it wasn't served with rice...

492
00:44:06,264 --> 00:44:08,264
まだまだこれから料理が出てくるから
...is because there are still more dishes coming.

493
00:44:08,764 --> 00:44:10,764
ひとまずいただきましょう
For now, let me eat!

494
00:44:12,764 --> 00:44:14,464
辛くはないよね？
It's not spicy, right?

495
00:44:15,264 --> 00:44:18,764
種類までは分からないけどアロマティックスパイスが効いてる
I don't know the exact ingredients, but the aromatic spices are really effective.

496
00:44:19,764 --> 00:44:22,264
あれに似てる！
Ah, it's like that!

497
00:44:22,264 --> 00:44:23,264
イカ！
Squid!

498
00:44:23,764 --> 00:44:25,764
干しイカ！
Dried squid!

499
00:44:26,764 --> 00:44:29,764
さきイカならぬさきチキンだね
It's like dried chicken instead of dried squid.

500
00:44:30,764 --> 00:44:33,264
すごく合いそう…
It seems like it would go so well...

501
00:44:33,264 --> 00:44:35,264
お酒と相性がすごく良さそう
It seems like it would go great with alcohol!

502
00:44:35,264 --> 00:44:37,264
ビールと一緒にね
Together with beer!

503
00:44:37,764 --> 00:44:40,764
おつまみに良さそうだね
It seems great as a snack to go with drinks!

504
00:44:42,064 --> 00:44:45,264
Ooh, and now the main dishes are out!

505
00:44:46,464 --> 00:44:50,064
This is Ayam Sambal Matah!

506
00:44:50,064 --> 00:44:51,764
Ayam Sambal Matah.

507
00:44:51,764 --> 00:44:53,764
Ayamが鶏肉のことで
Ayam means chicken...

508
00:44:53,764 --> 00:44:56,264
Sambal Matah生調味料のことだよ
...and Sambal Matah is a raw condiment dish.

509
00:44:51,764 --> 00:44:58,764
サンバ？！
Samba?!

510
00:44:48,764 --> 00:45:00,264
踊りの？
The dance?

511
00:44:50,264 --> 00:45:02,264
SambaじゃなくてSambalね
It's Sambal, not Samba.

512
00:45:02,272 --> 00:45:04,072
SambaじゃなくてSambalね
It's Sambal, not Samba.

513
00:45:04,072 --> 00:45:05,372
辛い調味料だよ
It's a spicy seasoning.

514
00:45:05,372 --> 00:45:10,272
生の素材を細かく刻んでいて
Fresh, raw ingredients are finely chopped,

515
00:45:10,272 --> 00:45:13,172
酸味と辛味を生かしつつ
creating a sour and spicy flavor,

516
00:45:13,172 --> 00:45:19,272
熱いオイルをかけて仕上げるの
and topped off with hot oil.

517
00:45:24,072 --> 00:45:26,072
これはお肉だよね？
Is this meat?

518
00:45:26,072 --> 00:45:28,072
鶏肉だよ
It's chicken meat.

519
00:45:31,072 --> 00:45:33,772
食べたことがある味がする！
I've tasted this before!

520
00:45:33,772 --> 00:45:37,072
インドネシアの麺料理かな
Like Indonesian noodles!

521
00:45:38,772 --> 00:45:42,072
言われてみれば似ているものがあるね
Now that you mention it, there is a similar flavor.

522
00:45:42,772 --> 00:45:45,272
私の好物の軟骨だよ
This is cartilage, my favorite!

523
00:45:45,272 --> 00:45:48,272
もっと食レポに集中しなきゃなんだろうけど
We're supposed to give a food review,

524
00:45:48,272 --> 00:45:51,072
美味しすぎて食べることしかできない
but it's so good, all I can do is eat!

525
00:45:51,272 --> 00:45:53,772
しょうがないよね
Can't be helped, right?

526
00:45:54,072 --> 00:45:56,072
私も軟骨を食べてみよっと
I'll try the cartilage too!

527
00:45:56,072 --> 00:45:58,772
軟骨はどこかな？
Where is the cartilage?

528
00:46:06,772 --> 00:46:09,772
Sambalに使われているオニオン食べてみる？
Want to try the onions in the Sambal?

529
00:46:13,772 --> 00:46:16,772
生だけじゃなくオニオンフライもあるよ
There are fried onions in addition to fresh ones.

530
00:46:16,772 --> 00:46:19,272
ミーゴレンみたいな味がする
It tastes like Mie Goreng!

531
00:46:19,272 --> 00:46:23,272
確かに酸味を感じられるね
You can definitely taste the sourness.

532
00:46:23,272 --> 00:46:25,072
辛さはあんまりないね
It's not really spicy.

533
00:46:25,072 --> 00:46:29,772
辛味というより塩味があるよね
Rather than spicy, it's more salty.

534
00:46:29,772 --> 00:46:33,272
インドネシアには色んな種類のSambalがあって
Indonesia has many types of Sambal,

535
00:46:33,272 --> 00:46:35,472
これとはまた違う種類もあるから
including ones different from this,

536
00:46:35,472 --> 00:46:39,272
機会があれば他の種類も試してほしいな
so I hope you try other kinds if you get the chance.

537
00:47:02,772 --> 00:47:05,272
そろそろ辛いのが食べたいでしょ
You want to eat something spicy by now, right?

538
00:47:05,272 --> 00:47:07,272
早く食べたいから食べていい？
Can I go ahead and eat this now?

539
00:47:07,272 --> 00:47:09,272
これがピーナッツソースなんだけど
This is peanut sauce,

540
00:47:09,272 --> 00:47:11,272
すっごく美味しいんだよ
and it's super delicious!

541
00:47:11,272 --> 00:47:15,772
鶏肉をピーナッツソースで食べたことないや
I've never eaten chicken with peanut sauce before.

542
00:47:20,272 --> 00:47:22,772
今日は鶏肉をたくさん食べてるね！
We're eating a lot of chicken today!

543
00:47:22,772 --> 00:47:26,772
インドネシア料理は鶏肉をよく使うよね
Chicken is used a lot in Indonesian cuisine, right?

544
00:47:32,772 --> 00:47:35,272
すごくクリーミーだね
It's super creamy.

545
00:47:35,272 --> 00:47:39,772
ピーナッツソース以外でも甘い醤油を使うこともあるんだよ
Besides peanut sauce, they sometimes use sweet soy sauce too.

546
00:47:40,272 --> 00:47:43,272
同じ鶏肉でも味付けが全然違うよね
Even with the same chicken, the flavor is completely different.

547
00:47:43,272 --> 00:47:45,272
調味料でかなり変わるよね
The seasonings really change it, don't they?

548
00:47:45,272 --> 00:47:48,272
次はどれを食べたい？
Which one do you want to try next?

549
00:47:53,272 --> 00:47:57,772
日常的によく食べられるのは鶏肉だけど
Chicken is what people usually eat the most,

550
00:47:57,772 --> 00:48:02,272
牛肉やラム肉は珍しいけど美味しいよね
but beef and lamb are also delicious even if they're uncommon.

551
00:48:10,272 --> 00:48:12,272
ビーフすっごく美味しいね！
The beef is super delicious!

552
00:48:16,272 --> 00:48:20,272
エビ好きだよ〜
I love shrimp~

553
00:48:20,272 --> 00:48:22,272
尻尾も食べる？
Do you eat the tail too?

554
00:48:22,272 --> 00:48:24,772
多分？どうだろう？
Maybe? Who knows?

555
00:48:34,272 --> 00:48:38,772
エビはエビだけどなんか違う
It's shrimp, but different from usual shrimp.

556
00:48:38,772 --> 00:48:42,272
味付けが通常のSateと違って
The seasoning is different from regular Sate,

557
00:48:42,272 --> 00:48:45,272
ピーナッツソースとかの定番じゃないけどすごく美味しい
it's not the usual peanut sauce, but it's really delicious!

558
00:48:51,072 --> 00:48:54,272
バイバイ オニオーン
Bye-bye, onion!

559
00:48:56,272 --> 00:49:00,772
ラムもピーナッツソースじゃないんだね
The lamb doesn't use peanut sauce either, huh?

560
00:49:02,272 --> 00:49:04,272
なんの味だろう？
I wonder what flavor this is?

561
00:49:04,272 --> 00:49:11,272
甘味が強い感じのソースだね
It's a sauce with a strong sweet note.

562
00:49:12,272 --> 00:49:13,272
レッツゴースパイシー
Let's go spicy!

563
00:49:13,272 --> 00:49:15,272
水飲むからちょっと待って
Hold on, I need a drink of water.

564
00:49:29,272 --> 00:49:32,272
甘辛い感じかな…
It's kind of sweet and spicy...

565
00:49:32,772 --> 00:49:36,772
あ、後から辛さがくるやつだ
Ah, it's the type where the spiciness kicks in later.

566
00:49:38,272 --> 00:49:41,772
本当だ！じわじわ辛さがくる
You're right! The spiciness slowly builds up.

567
00:49:41,772 --> 00:49:43,272
美味しくて好きだけどね
But it's delicious and I like it.

568
00:49:43,272 --> 00:49:45,272
あ〜辛い
Ah~ it's spicy!

569
00:49:45,272 --> 00:49:49,272
どの調味料か分からないけどすごく美味しい
I don't know what seasoning this is, but it's super delicious.

570
00:49:50,272 --> 00:49:53,772
5種類のうちどれが1番好きだった？
Out of the five kinds, which one was your favorite?

571
00:49:53,772 --> 00:49:56,772
エビのやつが好き！
I like the shrimp one!

572
00:49:57,272 --> 00:49:59,272
私は牛肉のSateが1番気に入ったかな
I think I liked the beef Sate the best.

573
00:49:59,272 --> 00:50:02,272
これまであまり牛肉のSateを食べたことがなかったからだと思うけど
Probably because I hadn't eaten beef Sate very often before.

574
00:50:02,280 --> 00:50:04,080
これまで あまり牛肉のSateを 食べたことがなかったからだと思うけど
I hadn't really eaten beef satay much before, but...

575
00:50:04,080 --> 00:50:07,780
すっごくおいしかった！
It was super delicious!

576
00:50:08,080 --> 00:50:13,980
まだ料理があるよ！
We have more food!

577
00:50:13,980 --> 00:50:16,880
かなり量の料理があるから ライスをもらえなかったのかな
Maybe that's why they didn't give us rice since there's so much food.

578
00:50:16,880 --> 00:50:19,080
さっきの鶏肉のSateがまだ辛い！
The chicken satay from earlier is still spicy!

579
00:50:19,080 --> 00:50:21,680
これは辛くないから大丈夫だよ
This one isn't spicy, so it's okay.

580
00:50:21,680 --> 00:50:25,480
ミーゴレンだよ！
This is Mi Goreng!

581
00:50:25,480 --> 00:50:28,780
前にインスタントのミーゴレンを食べたでしょ？
You ate instant Mi Goreng before, right?

582
00:50:28,780 --> 00:50:32,080
これは本格的なやつだよ
This is the real, non-instant version.

583
00:50:32,080 --> 00:50:35,680
これが辛くなくてよかった...
I'm so glad this isn't spicy...

584
00:50:35,680 --> 00:50:38,680
辛い食べ物は大好きだけど
I love spicy food, but...

585
00:50:38,680 --> 00:50:42,280
ちょっと休憩したかったから
I wanted a bit of a break.

586
00:50:42,280 --> 00:50:44,780
もちもちしてる！
It's nice and chewy!

587
00:50:44,780 --> 00:50:46,980
太麺だね！
And they're thick noodles!

588
00:50:46,980 --> 00:50:49,580
麺の食感がなんていうか...
The texture of the noodles is, how should I say...

589
00:50:49,580 --> 00:50:52,280
アニョアニョ
Very "enyal-enyal".

590
00:50:52,280 --> 00:50:53,580
アニョアニョ？
"Enyal-enyal"?

591
00:50:53,580 --> 00:50:55,880
インドネシア語でもちもちっていう意味だよ
It's Indonesian for "chewy"!

592
00:50:55,880 --> 00:51:00,480
可愛い！
Ah, it's cute!

593
00:51:00,480 --> 00:51:02,880
あにょあにょだよ～
It's "anyo-anyo"~

594
00:51:02,880 --> 00:51:08,580
各家庭でミーゴレンの味があるんだけど ここのミーゴレンすごく好きだな
Every household has its own Mi Goreng flavor, but I really like this style.

595
00:51:08,580 --> 00:51:10,480
焼きそばと似てるよね
It's like yakisoba, right?

596
00:51:10,480 --> 00:51:12,180
インドネシアの焼きそばだね
It's Indonesian yakisoba.

597
00:51:12,180 --> 00:51:16,480
甘めの焼きそばって感じ
It feels like a sweeter version of yakisoba.

598
00:51:16,480 --> 00:51:19,880
最初に納豆のいとこを食べて
First we had natto's cousin,

599
00:51:19,880 --> 00:51:24,080
今は焼きそばのいとこを食べてるね
and now we're eating yakisoba's cousin.

600
00:51:24,980 --> 00:51:33,080
最後に、これは「ラワール」というバリ島の伝統料理だよ
And finally, this is a traditional Balinese dish called Lawar.

601
00:51:33,080 --> 00:51:35,980
私も食べたことがなかったんだよね
I'd actually never eaten this before either.

602
00:51:35,980 --> 00:51:41,080
今日が初めてだからすごく楽しみ！
Today is my first time, so I'm really looking forward to it!

603
00:51:41,080 --> 00:51:44,280
まずピーナッツがあるでしょ
First, there are peanuts, right?

604
00:51:44,280 --> 00:51:45,980
これピーナッツか！
Oh, these are peanuts!

605
00:51:45,980 --> 00:51:49,080
納豆かと思ってた！違ったや
I thought it was natto! Turns out it wasn't.

606
00:51:49,080 --> 00:51:52,280
そしてインゲンね
And then string beans.

607
00:51:52,280 --> 00:52:02,280
インゲンは英語で何ていうのかな？
How do you say "ingen" in English?

608
00:52:02,280 --> 00:52:08,380
豚肉が使われることが多いんだけど
Usually, pork is used in this,

609
00:52:08,380 --> 00:52:17,080
ハラール仕様で鶏肉が使われているね
but because this is a halal version, they used chicken instead.

610
00:52:17,080 --> 00:52:24,280
どんな味がするのか楽しみ！食べてみよう！
I wonder what it tastes like, so excited! Let me try it!

611
00:52:24,280 --> 00:52:28,280
インゲンから食べてみるね
I'll try the string beans first.

612
00:52:28,280 --> 00:52:32,280
インゲンがサクサクしていていいね
The string beans are nice and crunchy.

613
00:52:32,280 --> 00:52:34,680
スナックみたいだね
It's like a snack!

614
00:52:34,680 --> 00:52:37,580
確かにスナック菓子っぽいね
Yeah, it really is like a snack.

615
00:52:37,580 --> 00:52:42,080
塩味も効いてる おやつにつまみたい！
It's nice and salty! I'd love to eat this as a snack!

616
00:52:42,080 --> 00:52:45,280
美味しい！
It's delicious!

617
00:52:46,480 --> 00:52:49,780
めっちゃいっぱい食べたね！
We ate so much food!

618
00:52:49,780 --> 00:52:52,080
おなかは大丈夫？
Is your stomach doing okay?

619
00:52:52,080 --> 00:52:56,880
ちゃんと別腹は空いてる？
Do you still have room in your dessert stomach?

620
00:52:56,880 --> 00:52:59,480
デザートも入るよね？
You can still eat dessert, right?

621
00:52:59,480 --> 00:53:03,280
デザートの時間だよ！！！
It's time for dessert!!!

622
00:53:03,280 --> 00:53:11,280
マンゴープリンだよ！
It's mango pudding!

623
00:53:11,280 --> 00:53:15,880
この下にあるのはチョコかな？
Is that chocolate at the bottom?

624
00:53:15,880 --> 00:53:18,080
砂糖か何かかな？
Or maybe sugar or something?

625
00:53:18,080 --> 00:53:20,480
食べて確かめよう
Let's taste it to find out.

626
00:53:30,280 --> 00:53:32,780
すごくやわらかいね
It's so soft!

627
00:53:35,480 --> 00:53:42,080
すごくクリーミー！
It's so creamy!

628
00:53:42,080 --> 00:53:49,280
確信はないけどこのクリーミーさは ココナッツミルクかな？
I'm not sure, but maybe this creaminess comes from coconut milk?

629
00:53:51,480 --> 00:53:55,480
この下のブラウンのものは何？
What is this brown stuff at the bottom?

630
00:53:55,480 --> 00:53:59,080
さっきからその部分が気になってるんだよね
I've been curious about that part for a while.

631
00:53:59,080 --> 00:54:02,280
私にとらせてね
Let me get some for you.

632
00:54:12,780 --> 00:54:14,380
キャラメル味だ
It tastes like caramel.

633
00:54:14,380 --> 00:54:18,080
キャラメルソースだね！
It's caramel sauce!

634
00:54:21,780 --> 00:54:25,480
もう１つデザートがあるみたいだよ
Looks like there's another dessert!

635
00:54:25,480 --> 00:54:32,480
揚げバナナだよ！
It's fried bananas!

636
00:54:32,480 --> 00:54:38,080
バナナにバターを付けたりして 衣をつけるんだよ
You coat the banana in batter and deep-fry it.

637
00:54:38,080 --> 00:54:40,480
絶対に美味しいジャン
That has got to be delicious!

638
00:54:40,480 --> 00:54:48,280
インドネシアでは定番のおやつだね
It's a classic snack in Indonesia.

639
00:54:48,280 --> 00:54:54,480
アイスと一緒に食べることはあまりないけど ファンシーだから不満はないよ
We don't usually eat it with ice cream, but it's fancy so no complaints!

640
00:54:54,480 --> 00:54:58,480
すごくいい匂いがするね
It smells so good!

641
00:54:58,480 --> 00:54:59,936
※バナナが熱々です
*The banana is extremely hot!*

642
00:55:02,088 --> 00:55:04,188
あ、熱っ！
Ow, hot!

643
00:55:12,888 --> 00:55:13,488
熱い！
It's hot!

644
00:55:13,588 --> 00:55:16,688
バターが染みていて美味しいね
I think the butter is soaked in and delicious.

645
00:55:16,688 --> 00:55:19,688
It's the best!!!

646
00:55:20,188 --> 00:55:24,088
甘さ控えてちょうどいい
It's sweet, but not too sweet.

647
00:55:24,088 --> 00:55:28,088
アップルパイっぽい感じ
It feels like apple pie.

648
00:55:29,088 --> 00:55:33,788
カメラロールが黙々と食べているだけの私たちの映像でいっぱいになってるよね
The camera roll is going to be full of videos of us just silently eating.

649
00:55:39,288 --> 00:55:41,788
完食 / Finished
[Finished]

650
00:55:42,488 --> 00:55:44,888
今日は来てくれて本当にありがとう！
Thank you so much for coming today!

651
00:55:44,888 --> 00:55:47,088
招待してくれてありがとう！
Thank you so much for inviting me!

652
00:55:47,588 --> 00:55:49,888
どうだった？ 楽しかったよ〜
How was it? - It was so fun~

653
00:55:49,888 --> 00:55:52,788
私もしとっても楽しかったよ
I had so much fun too!

654
00:55:52,988 --> 00:55:55,988
今日はたくさんのインドネシア料理を食べたけど
We ate a lot of Indonesian food today, but...

655
00:55:55,988 --> 00:55:58,488
次は what do we do?
Next, what do we do?

656
00:55:58,488 --> 00:56:00,188
もっとレベルを上げるために！
To level up even more!

657
00:56:00,188 --> 00:56:04,488
インドネシアへ行くよ！
Let me go to Indonesia!

658
00:56:04,488 --> 00:56:07,688
インドネシア料理が好きになったよ
I've come to love Indonesian food!

659
00:56:07,688 --> 00:56:10,788
料理の次は実際にインドネシアへ行こう
After the food, let's actually go to Indonesia!

660
00:56:10,788 --> 00:56:15,788
インドネシア料理を作るよ！
I'll make Indonesian food!

661
00:56:15,788 --> 00:56:19,088
はあちゃまのインドネシア料理
Haachama's Indonesian cooking!

662
00:56:19,088 --> 00:56:22,088
お願いがあるんだけど…
I have a favor to ask, though...

663
00:56:22,088 --> 00:56:26,788
日本のローカルな食事を食べに連れて行って
Take me out to eat local Japanese food.

664
00:56:26,788 --> 00:56:30,088
日本のみんなが普段どんなものを食べているのか知りたい
I want to know what everyone in Japan usually eats.

665
00:56:30,088 --> 00:56:31,288
私が教えてあげるよ
I'll teach you!

666
00:56:31,288 --> 00:56:33,488
日常的な食事を味わってみたい〜
I want to taste everyday meals~

667
00:56:33,488 --> 00:56:35,288
Yummy

668
00:56:35,788 --> 00:56:40,688
ということでみんな！ 今後もはあちゃまとレイネのアドベンチャーを楽しみにしててね！
So everyone, look forward to more of Haachama and Reine's adventures!

669
00:56:40,688 --> 00:56:43,288
ということでスタジオへ戻しましょう
So with that, let's head back to the studio!

670
00:56:43,288 --> 00:56:45,888
Studio Reine, are you there?

671
00:56:45,888 --> 00:56:49,088
スタジオのレイネさ〜ん 取れますかぁ〜？
Reine-san in the studio, can you hear us~?

672
00:56:50,788 --> 00:56:54,088
はい！スタジオのレイネです！
Yes! This is Reine in the studio!

673
00:56:54,288 --> 00:57:00,188
So, what did you think of our trip to the Indonesian restaurant in Japan with Haachama?

674
00:57:00,288 --> 00:57:04,188
Oh, that looks so delicious! I want to go!

675
00:57:04,288 --> 00:57:07,688
I'll take you guys there next time. - Please! Food, food, food!

676
00:57:07,688 --> 00:57:10,788
I'm getting hungry!

677
00:57:10,788 --> 00:57:14,088
All right, next up, let's play our second game!

678
00:57:14,088 --> 00:57:15,788
Yay! Okay!

679
00:57:15,788 --> 00:57:21,188
Well, just like in game one, we will be competing to see who can reach the goal the fastest.

680
00:57:21,288 --> 00:57:23,288
Yeah, okay. Are you guys ready?

681
00:57:23,288 --> 00:57:28,688
No! For this game, we will be using this item!

682
00:57:28,788 --> 00:57:34,288
Okay! Oh wow, a beach ball! Yay!

683
00:57:34,288 --> 00:57:40,088
Man, I wish I was a baller, I wish I was a little bit taller, I wish I had a 6'4" Impala...

684
00:57:40,288 --> 00:57:43,488
...or a girl who looked cute, I would call her.

685
00:57:43,788 --> 00:57:48,288
Woah, the violence! I'm bullying the camera! This isn't soccer, all right? Knock that off.

686
00:57:48,788 --> 00:57:51,088
The cup is over. - Okay, okay, okay!

687
00:57:51,288 --> 00:57:55,288
The rules for the next game are super simple.

688
00:57:55,288 --> 00:58:00,288
You hold this ball between your legs like you're giving birth!

689
00:58:00,288 --> 00:58:06,788
Yeah, so like this...

690
00:58:06,788 --> 00:58:11,088
And then, you guys will be racing while hopping!

691
00:58:11,088 --> 00:58:15,788
Aw, I thought we were gonna play football. - No, you're not! Next time, next year, football.

692
00:58:15,788 --> 00:58:19,788
Let's go, let's go! Football next year, let's go.

693
00:58:19,788 --> 00:58:24,288
And the game is called the Bola Challenge!

694
00:58:24,288 --> 00:58:26,788
Bola means ball. - Bola Challenge!

695
00:58:26,788 --> 00:58:30,788
Bola, bola! Who got the biggest ball?

696
00:58:30,788 --> 00:58:34,288
Mine's definitely small, just because of the skirt situation.

697
00:58:34,288 --> 00:58:39,788
Oh, so that's why! Yeah, small ball. Hey, hey, stop.

698
00:58:41,288 --> 00:58:44,288
ボールを足の間に挟んで跳び、スタートからゴールまでのタイムを競う
Hold the ball between your legs and hop from start to finish.

699
00:58:44,288 --> 00:58:48,288
Start there, hop to the turnaround point, and make it to the finish line, right?

700
00:58:48,288 --> 00:58:52,288
Simple, right? - Yeah, very simple!

701
00:58:52,288 --> 00:58:55,288
Yeah, okay. Well, there's a twist, actually.

702
00:58:55,288 --> 00:59:00,288
To make things more interesting, we're adding two extra rules.

703
00:59:01,288 --> 00:59:06,788
ただし、レース中は「お題」に沿った会話をし続けてください
However, you must keep talking about the given topic throughout the race.

704
00:59:06,788 --> 00:59:11,288
Oh! Yeah, so it's just like, you guys are good at yapping, right?

705
00:59:11,288 --> 00:59:15,788
I guess so! - Yeah, now you can do that while...

706
00:59:15,788 --> 00:59:18,288
While jumping? I never tried yapping while balling.

707
00:59:18,288 --> 00:59:22,788
Never too late to pick up a new skill!

708
00:59:22,788 --> 00:59:25,288
Put it on your resume.

709
00:59:25,288 --> 00:59:31,288
And just like before, two people will compete at a time, so make sure you keep chatting with your opponent while you race.

710
00:59:31,288 --> 00:59:36,288
All right, the yapping has... Woah, are you okay?

711
00:59:36,288 --> 00:59:40,288
Are you okay? - I tried doing a trick, I failed!

712
00:59:40,288 --> 00:59:44,288
Go on!

713
00:59:47,288 --> 00:59:50,288
折り返し地点を過ぎたら、相手の邪魔をしてもOKです
After the turnaround, you're allowed to mess with your opponent!

714
00:59:50,288 --> 00:59:55,288
So if you want to tickle your opponent... - Yeah, exactly!

715
00:59:55,288 --> 01:00:00,288
Hey! I'm not gonna do that to you... - Yeah, basically like that.

716
01:00:01,296 --> 01:00:03,096
I tried this during rehearsal,

717
01:00:03,096 --> 01:00:05,796
well, I tried, and I guess it's got to be,
Well, I tried, and I guess it's gonna be...

718
01:00:05,796 --> 01:00:08,796
you know, it's kind of tiring, so it's your choice basically.

719
01:00:09,296 --> 01:00:11,796
You can just like focus on racing, or, you know, if you can,

720
01:00:11,796 --> 01:00:16,296
you're a little bit mischievous, you want to tickle, you want to tickle your opponent.
you're a little bit mischievous, you want to tickle your opponent.

721
01:00:16,296 --> 01:00:19,096
Yeah, you want to, yeah, you want to lift them up and kiss them, that's fine too.
Yeah, you want to lift them up and kiss them, that's fine too.

722
01:00:19,296 --> 01:00:21,296
Are you ticklish? / I'm not ticklish.

723
01:00:21,296 --> 01:00:23,296
I'm not...

724
01:00:23,296 --> 01:00:26,296
Liar! I think she might be ticklish.

725
01:00:26,296 --> 01:00:28,796
No, I'm not ticklish at all. Hiding something. / Wait, now use it to your advantage!

726
01:00:29,296 --> 01:00:32,296
Never let your opponent know your weakness.

727
01:00:32,296 --> 01:00:34,296
No, no, no, no.

728
01:00:34,296 --> 01:00:38,296
But anyway, alright, everybody, let's get into position. Calli and Kiara?

729
01:00:38,296 --> 01:00:40,796
Oh boy, I'm first again! / Yeah, that's fine.

730
01:00:40,796 --> 01:00:44,296
Let's go. You're already getting started. Don't make it too hard for yourself.

731
01:00:44,296 --> 01:00:47,296
Yeah, you make it harder for yourself.

732
01:00:47,296 --> 01:00:49,796
Wait, what's our topic?

733
01:00:49,796 --> 01:00:53,796
Wait, wait, wait, hold on, hold on. I'm gonna go here first. Ooh!

734
01:00:53,796 --> 01:00:55,296
Can we talk?

735
01:00:55,296 --> 01:00:57,796
Okay, your topic is...

736
01:00:57,796 --> 01:01:00,796
Things I love about my cat!

737
01:01:00,796 --> 01:01:04,296
Ah! Easy, right? Nekochima! / That's a pretty easy one!

738
01:01:04,296 --> 01:01:08,296
You guys both have adorable cats at home, so go ahead and brag as much as you want!

739
01:01:08,796 --> 01:01:10,796
Okay. Right?

740
01:01:11,796 --> 01:01:14,796
Okay, that might actually help me forget that I'm tired.

741
01:01:14,796 --> 01:01:17,796
Oh, yeah, cats take that all away.

742
01:01:17,796 --> 01:01:20,296
So fluffy. What about... can we talk about that cat over there?

743
01:01:20,296 --> 01:01:22,796
No!

744
01:01:22,796 --> 01:01:26,296
Focus on your game! That's a secret agent disguised as a cat!

745
01:01:28,296 --> 01:01:31,296
True, true, true. Or a cat disguised as a secret agent.

746
01:01:32,796 --> 01:01:34,296
Are you guys ready?

747
01:01:34,296 --> 01:01:36,296
Yeah, ready as I'll ever be.

748
01:01:36,296 --> 01:01:41,796
All right. On your marks... 3, 2, 1, go!

749
01:01:42,296 --> 01:01:45,296
Chutu is so fluffy and cute! She has the most adorable black stripe...

750
01:01:45,296 --> 01:01:49,296
right down the back of her... What are you doing?!

751
01:01:49,296 --> 01:01:53,296
Her tail is so fluffy and long! / No, no, no!

752
01:01:53,296 --> 01:01:56,296
No, Calli!

753
01:01:56,296 --> 01:01:59,296
Should we increase the distance?

754
01:01:59,296 --> 01:02:02,296
Should we make it a little further? / Wait, do I have to finish it?

755
01:02:04,796 --> 01:02:08,296
Well, tell me a little bit about your cats, Kiara. / That's all?

756
01:02:08,296 --> 01:02:12,296
Currently, um, I'm not with my cats, so that makes me really sad.

757
01:02:12,296 --> 01:02:16,296
But, um, my cat caretakers are sending me videos of them,

758
01:02:16,296 --> 01:02:19,796
and they're sleeping like on the towels, even though I said, "Don't sleep on the towels."

759
01:02:19,796 --> 01:02:23,296
Because the towels are not supposed to have cat hair all over.

760
01:02:23,296 --> 01:02:26,296
But it's okay, I forgive them. I'll just buy new towels, so there's cat towels and human towels.

761
01:02:26,296 --> 01:02:29,296
That's a good idea to separate them like that. / Oh, Calli!

762
01:02:29,796 --> 01:02:33,296
That is so good!

763
01:02:33,296 --> 01:02:36,296
Nice job! Good job!

764
01:02:36,296 --> 01:02:39,296
That is so good! Oh my.

765
01:02:39,296 --> 01:02:42,796
Well done, well done. I respect the legwork, that was intense.

766
01:02:42,796 --> 01:02:46,296
I mean, this is... I actually do this during my training anyway.

767
01:02:46,296 --> 01:02:49,796
Yeah, hold the ball between my legs and jump, so I kind of had an unfair advantage.

768
01:02:49,796 --> 01:02:52,796
Oh, so you're... okay, you built up that skill.

769
01:02:52,796 --> 01:02:55,296
Every muscle training session. / You trained the balling!

770
01:02:55,296 --> 01:02:58,296
Okay, ultra!

771
01:02:58,296 --> 01:03:01,296
Let's announce your times, girls!

772
01:03:01,296 --> 01:03:05,796
Let me replay! Let's go, let's go, let's go! No, your turn! / Ganbatte, ganbatte!

773
01:03:06,296 --> 01:03:09,296
Well, I wonder who won?

774
01:03:09,296 --> 01:03:12,796
That was a close one! / It was a close match.

775
01:03:12,796 --> 01:03:15,796
It was very, very close!

776
01:03:16,296 --> 01:03:19,296
Okay, silence please. All right!

777
01:03:19,796 --> 01:03:21,796
So...

778
01:03:23,796 --> 01:03:28,796
It's close! Can you say my time first? / Okay, your time first, okay, okay, let's see.

779
01:03:28,796 --> 01:03:34,796
Kiara, your time was 46.5 seconds!

780
01:03:34,796 --> 01:03:39,296
Yay! That's crazy!

781
01:03:39,296 --> 01:03:42,796
That's a crazy dance move! / Yeah!

782
01:03:42,796 --> 01:03:46,296
That's crazy, crazy dance moves! She sure knows how to throw down!

783
01:03:46,296 --> 01:03:49,296
And yours... / Okay, now Calli...

784
01:03:49,296 --> 01:03:52,296
It was a close one. / Yeah, yeah, yeah.

785
01:03:52,296 --> 01:03:56,796
Your time was 10.5 seconds!

786
01:03:56,796 --> 01:04:03,296
(Laughs) Ooh!

787
01:04:03,296 --> 01:04:06,296
I could have been a little faster, I guess. / Oh man.

788
01:04:06,296 --> 01:04:09,796
This is me on slow days.

789
01:04:09,796 --> 01:04:12,296
Good job, Kiara. / Yeah, I need to...

790
01:04:12,296 --> 01:04:15,296
work on my feelings...

791
01:04:15,296 --> 01:04:18,796
How are you feeling? / How are you feeling?

792
01:04:18,796 --> 01:04:21,796
I had an unfair advantage... / I just wish I was a baller!

793
01:04:22,296 --> 01:04:25,296
Well, first you gotta be a little bit taller.

794
01:04:25,296 --> 01:04:28,796
By a 6'4 Impala. Then we'll talk.

795
01:04:28,796 --> 01:04:32,296
Well, I hope that your match will be a little bit closer.

796
01:04:32,296 --> 01:04:36,296
Ganbatte! Good match, Calli! / Mhm, okay. Yeah!

797
01:04:36,296 --> 01:04:39,796
Ganbatte! / You guys are up! Ganba, ganba!

798
01:04:39,796 --> 01:04:42,296
Take your ball! / Okay, sorry, my ball.

799
01:04:42,296 --> 01:04:44,796
Get your ball! / So I left my ball...

800
01:04:44,796 --> 01:04:48,296
